The good news is that there will be no pink slips for teachers in March, Superintendent Kevin Skelly said. With enrollment growing, the district will hire fewer teachers than usual but does not plan on laying any off.
��Avoiding layoffs is a high priority,�� Skelly said, noting that the district has invested substantial time and money training its teachers. ��We��re pleased that we don��t need to do that at this time.��
